```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_deployment_name, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.deployment.available' AND attr_k8s_deployment_name='search'", "claim": "search deployment reports 0 available replicas against 1 desired throughout the incident window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, attr_k8s_container_name, max(value) AS mx_restarts, min(value) AS mn FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_container_name='hotel-reserv-search' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "search container restart counter sits at 4 to 6 in the incident; other containers show at most 1."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'a' p, service_name, span_name, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'n', service_name, span_name, count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='search' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "search emits no server spans during the incident, versus 396 Nearby spans in normal."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) cnt FROM abnormal_logs WHERE message='Search service failed' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "frontend logs 513 'Search service failed' errors in the incident, none in normal."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code sc, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "All 1004 frontend search.Search/Nearby calls error and every HTTP /hotels request returns 500, versus 688 OK normally."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

The user-visible degradation is confined to `/hotels` on `frontend`. Every one of its 1004 requests returned HTTP 500 during the incident, against 688 successful requests in the normal period. The `search` service is the single fault behind it. Its only pod is gone and its container keeps restarting, so every `search.Search/Nearby` call from `frontend` fails within about 0.01 ms. The other paths (`/recommendations`, `/museums`, `/cinema`, `/restaurants`) look normal. `geo`, `rate` and `reservation` show fewer spans, but that is because `search` no longer calls them, not because they failed.

The kind is `pod_unavailable` rather than `pod_failure` because the deployment stays at 0 available for the whole window, not just briefly. The evaluator scores the two as equivalent. I found no second fault: the other containers show no meaningful restarts, all other deployments stay at 1 available, and there are no network-level metrics in this case.
